{"entryType":"UniProtKB unreviewed (TrEMBL)","primaryAccession":"A0A286ZZ96","secondaryAccessions":["A0A4X1W3V9"],"uniProtkbId":"A0A286ZZ96_PIG","entryAudit":{"firstPublicDate":"2017-11-22","lastAnnotationUpdateDate":"2026-09-02","lastSequenceUpdateDate":"2017-11-22","entryVersion":53,"sequenceVersion":1},"annotationScore":5.0,"organism":{"scientificName":"Sus scrofa","commonName":"Pig","taxonId":9823,"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000313","source":"Ensembl","id":"ENSSSCP00000036792.1"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000313","source":"Proteomes","id":"UP000008227"}],"lineage":["Eukaryota","Metazoa","Chordata","Craniata","Vertebrata","Euteleostomi","Mammalia","Eutheria","Laurasiatheria","Artiodactyla","Suina","Suidae","Sus"]},"proteinExistence":"3: Inferred from homology","proteinDescription":{"recommendedName":{"fullName":{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000256","source":"ARBA","id":"ARBA00016668"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000256","source":"RuleBase","id":"RU362037"}],"value":"Cystic fibrosis transmembrane conductance regulator"},"ecNumbers":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000256","source":"ARBA","id":"ARBA00012195"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000256","source":"RuleBase","id":"RU362037"}],"value":"5.6.1.6"}]},"alternativeNames":[{"fullName":{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000256","source":"ARBA","id":"ARBA00029720"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000256","source":"RuleBase","id":"RU362037"}],"value":"ATP-binding cassette sub-family C member 7"}},{"fullName":{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000256","source":"ARBA","id":"ARBA00031358"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000256","source":"RuleBase","id":"RU362037"}],"value":"Channel conductance-controlling ATPase"}},{"fullName":{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000256","source":"ARBA","id":"ARBA00033163"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000256","source":"RuleBase","id":"RU362037"}],"value":"cAMP-dependent chloride channel"}}]},"genes":[{"geneName":{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000313","source":"Ensembl","id":"ENSSSCP00000036792.1"}],"value":"CFTR"}}],"comments":[{"texts":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000256","source":"RuleBase","id":"RU362037"}],"value":"Epithelial ion channel that plays an important role in the regulation of epithelial ion and water transport and fluid homeostasis. Mediates the transport of chloride ions across the cell membrane. Possesses an intrinsic ATPase activity and utilizes ATP to gate its channel; the passive flow of anions through the channel is gated by cycles of ATP binding and hydrolysis by the ATP-binding domains. The ion channel is also permeable to HCO(3)(-); selectivity depends on the extracellular chloride concentration. Exerts its function also by modulating the activity of other ion channels and transporters. Contributes to the regulation of the pH and the ion content of the epithelial fluid layer"}],"commentType":"FUNCTION"},{"commentType":"CATALYTIC ACTIVITY","reaction":{"name":"ATP + H2O + closed Cl(-) channel = ADP + phosphate + open Cl(-) channel.","ecNumber":"5.6.1.6","evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000256","source":"ARBA","id":"ARBA00034073"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000256","source":"RuleBase","id":"RU362037"}]}},{"commentType":"CATALYTIC ACTIVITY","reaction":{"name":"ATP + H2O = ADP + phosphate + H(+)","reactionCrossReferences":[{"database":"Rhea","id":"RHEA:13065"},{"database":"ChEBI","id":"CHEBI:15377"},{"database":"ChEBI","id":"CHEBI:15378"},{"database":"ChEBI","id":"CHEBI:30616"},{"database":"ChEBI","id":"CHEBI:43474"},{"database":"ChEBI","id":"CHEBI:456216"}],"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000256","source":"ARBA","id":"ARBA00048778"}]},"physiologicalReactions":[{"directionType":"left-to-right","reactionCrossReference":{"database":"Rhea","id":"RHEA:13066"},"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000256","source":"ARBA","id":"ARBA00048778"}]}]},{"commentType":"CATALYTIC ACTIVITY","reaction":{"name":"chloride(in) = chloride(out)","reactionCrossReferences":[{"database":"Rhea","id":"RHEA:29823"},{"database":"ChEBI","id":"CHEBI:17996"}],"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000256","source":"ARBA","id":"ARBA00024167"}]}},{"commentType":"CATALYTIC ACTIVITY","reaction":{"name":"hydrogencarbonate(in) = hydrogencarbonate(out)","reactionCrossReferences":[{"database":"Rhea","id":"RHEA:28695"},{"database":"ChEBI","id":"CHEBI:17544"}],"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000256","source":"ARBA","id":"ARBA00044653"}]}},{"texts":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000256","source":"ARBA","id":"ARBA00094716"}],"value":"Monomer; does not require oligomerization for channel activity. May form oligomers in the membrane. Interacts with SLC26A3, SLC26A6 and NHERF1. Interacts with SHANK2. Interacts with MYO6. Interacts (via C-terminus) with GOPC (via PDZ domain); this promotes CFTR internalization and thereby decreases channel activity. Interacts with SLC4A7 through NHERF1. Found in a complex with MYO5B and RAB11A. Interacts with ANO1. Interacts with SLC26A8. Interacts with AHCYL1; the interaction increases CFTR activity. Interacts with CSE1L. The core-glycosylated form interacts with GORASP2 (via PDZ GRASP-type 1 domain) in respone to ER stress. Interacts with MARCHF2; the interaction leads to CFTR ubiquitination and degradation. Interacts with ADGRG2"}],"commentType":"SUBUNIT"},{"commentType":"SUBCELLULAR LOCATION","subcellularLocations":[{"location":{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000256","source":"ARBA","id":"ARBA00004424"}],"value":"Apical cell membrane","id":"SL-0015"},"topology":{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000256","source":"ARBA","id":"ARBA00004424"}],"value":"Multi-pass membrane protein","id":"SL-9909"}},{"location":{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000256","source":"RuleBase","id":"RU362037"}],"value":"Cell membrane","id":"SL-0039"},"topology":{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000256","source":"RuleBase","id":"RU362037"}],"value":"Multi-pass membrane protein","id":"SL-9909"}},{"location":{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000256","source":"ARBA","id":"ARBA00004520"}],"value":"Early endosome membrane","id":"